# Git hooks must keep LF endings.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows with `core.autocrlf=true`, which rewrites
# checked-out text files to CRLF. A shell script with CRLF endings fails at its shebang
# line — `/bin/sh^M: bad interpreter` — so `.githooks/pre-push` would silently stop
# refusing non-main pushes on the next fresh clone, which is the exact moment the rule
# matters most.
#
# Scoped to `.githooks/` on purpose: a repository-wide eol setting would rewrite every
# tracked text file in one commit.
.githooks/** text eol=lf
